You are a senior Microsoft Security Copilot, Sentinel and Defender XDR automation
architect. Design and build a 24/7 "AI Triage and Close" workflow for a mid-size
company (~1,500 users, US/Canada/UK/EU) with Microsoft Sentinel in the unified
Defender portal, Defender for Endpoint, Entra ID P2, Intune, Jira, and Microsoft
Security Copilot (provisioned capacity, SCUs). There is no 24/7 SOC team.

GOAL
Use the Microsoft-built Security Copilot "Security Analyst Agent" to investigate
every HIGH and MEDIUM severity incident 24/7, then use a Logic App to act on the
agent's verdict: close false/benign positives automatically when strict safety
criteria are met, contain true positives (with approval for high-impact actions),
and escalate anything uncertain to a human. Low/informational incidents are out of
scope (already auto-closed by the MSSP orchestrator).

IMPORTANT: First confirm what the Security Analyst Agent can do today and how it can
be triggered (automatic in Defender, Security Copilot Logic App connector, promptbook,
or API). If the agent cannot be invoked from a Logic App, design the closest supported
alternative (Security Copilot connector "Submit a prompt" / "Submit a promptbook" with
a structured triage promptbook) and say clearly which parts are GA vs preview.

COVERAGE
- 24/7, every day.
- Business hours (Mon-Fri 07:00-18:00 Central): agent investigates, Logic App
  proposes the action, analyst confirms in Teams (human in the loop).
- After hours, weekends and holidays (watchlist "AI_Holidays"): agent investigates
  and the Logic App acts automatically within the safety rules below.
- Kill switches in watchlist "AI_Config": AIAutoCloseEnabled, HighEnabled,
  MediumEnabled, AfterHoursOnly (true/false).

WORKFLOW (Logic App, Consumption, new designer, triggered by a Sentinel automation
rule "When incident is created" with condition Severity = High OR Medium)
1. Trigger: Sentinel incident. Add tag "ai-triage" and comment "AI triage started".
2. Read kill switches and business-hours/holiday status.
3. Extract entities (accounts, hosts, IPs, URLs, hashes, mailboxes).
4. Invoke the Security Analyst Agent (or the triage promptbook) with the incident ID
   and entities. Require a structured JSON response:
   { verdict: TruePositive | BenignPositive | FalsePositive | Undetermined,
     confidence: 0-100, summary, evidence[], affected_entities[],
     recommended_actions[], mitre_techniques[], classification_reason }
5. Validate the JSON (Parse JSON with schema). If invalid, timeout, HTTP error, or the
   agent is unavailable -> fall back to the Sentinel-only playbook path, tag
   "ai-unavailable", notify on-call.
6. Post the agent summary and evidence as an incident comment.
7. Decision engine:

   A) AUTO-CLOSE (FalsePositive or BenignPositive) ONLY IF ALL are true:
      - confidence >= 90 for Medium, >= 95 for High
      - no entity in "AI_ExcludedAccounts" (break-glass, admins, executives/VIPs,
        service accounts) or "AI_ExcludedDevices" (DCs, SQL servers, critical servers)
      - no privileged role on involved accounts (check Entra role membership)
      - no other open incidents for the same entities in the last 24 hours
      - no malicious threat intelligence match on IPs/URLs/hashes
      - incident type is not on the "never auto-close" list (ransomware,
        credential theft from privileged accounts, data exfiltration, persistence
        on servers)
      Then close the incident in Sentinel with the correct classification
      (FalsePositive - IncorrectAlertLogic / BenignPositive - SuspiciousButExpected),
      add the agent reasoning as the closing comment, tag "ai-auto-closed",
      update Jira to Resolved.
      High severity auto-close: close but also tag "ai-closed-high-review" and add to
      the next-morning human review queue (mandatory review within 24h).

   B) TRUE POSITIVE:
      - Low-impact actions run automatically: revoke sessions, AV scan, add indicator,
        soft-delete phishing email, confirm user compromised.
      - High-impact actions (disable user, isolate device, restrict app execution)
        require Teams approval: timeout 15 minutes for High, 60 minutes for Medium.
      - On timeout: High identity -> safe default (revoke sessions + require password
        reset); devices -> never isolate on timeout, escalate by Teams call/phone.
        Medium -> no high-impact action, tag "ai-review", keep open.
      - Keep incident Active, assign to on-call, Jira priority Highest/High.

   C) UNDETERMINED or confidence below threshold:
      - Do not close. Tag "ai-needs-human", assign to on-call, Teams notification with
        the agent summary; Medium after hours -> next business morning queue;
        High -> immediate notification.

8. Execute actions via existing worker playbooks (child Logic Apps): Block user,
   Revoke sessions, Confirm risky user, Isolate/Unisolate device, AV scan, Restrict app.
9. Failure path: "Catch" scope -> comment with the error, tag "ai-failed", reopen if
   closed, raise severity, notify on-call.
10. Reopen safety net: a scheduled rule every hour that reopens any "ai-auto-closed"
    incident if a new alert appears for the same entities within 72 hours, tags
    "ai-reopened", and notifies on-call.
11. Audit: every step logged as an incident comment (agent verdict, confidence,
    decision rule matched, action, approver); tags by severity "ai-high"/"ai-medium";
    Jira issue created and kept in two-way sync (status, comments).
12. Daily and Monday reports (scheduled Logic App): per severity - incidents
    triaged, auto-closed, true positives, contained, undetermined, approvals,
    timeouts, reopened (false negatives), agent accuracy vs human review, SCU usage
    and cost. Post to Teams and email.

QUALITY CONTROL
- Human spot-check: 100% of High auto-closes and 10% random sample of Medium
  auto-closes reviewed weekly; record agree/disagree in a watchlist or table.
- Start thresholds conservative; only lower them if agreement >= 95% over 4 weeks.
- Track false negatives (reopened incidents) as the key safety metric.

COST AND RELIABILITY
- Only High/Medium trigger the agent; deduplicate incidents with the same entities
  within 30 minutes; set an SCU budget alert and a daily cap; if the cap is reached,
  fall back to the Sentinel-only path.
- Retry policy for Security Copilot calls (2 retries, exponential backoff).
- Note known issue: custom agent publishing at workspace scope returns HTTP 500;
  design must work with the built-in Security Analyst Agent or a promptbook.

SECURITY AND PERMISSIONS
- System-assigned managed identities, least privilege. List exact roles:
  Microsoft Sentinel Responder, Sentinel Automation Contributor, Security Copilot
  contributor/workspace access for the connector identity, Defender for Endpoint API
  (Machine.Isolate, Machine.Scan, Machine.RestrictExecution, Ti.ReadWrite),
  Microsoft Graph (User.RevokeSessions.All, IdentityRiskyUser.ReadWrite.All,
  RoleManagement.Read.Directory, User.EnableDisableAccount.All only if used).
- No secrets in workflows; Jira API token in Key Vault.
- The agent must never take actions directly; all actions go through the Logic App
  decision engine and worker playbooks.

